#
# Conformance case: teleology/contested-evaluations.
#
# Two vantages disagree about the same goal+situation: one authored logic:GoalEvaluation is Satisfied+Completed, the other Violated+Completed. BOTH records are retained (no global verdict); the forward bridge generates exactly ONE flat gmeow:satisfiedBy edge — for the satisfied vantage only — attributed to that vantage via gmeow:accordingTo.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/contested-evaluations/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
